1. 1st do integer division (a/b)
2. Then * multiply with 1.00

For the 1st case, as * and / both have the same precedence. But the compiler does it left to right.

---->>> In programming, operator precedence determines the order in which operators are evaluated in an expression. 
Left-to-right associativity means that operators with the same precedence are evaluated from left to right in the expression.

For the 2nd case,
We use () to do the a/b or integer division first. 

That's why the same problem occurs. We don't get the accurate result.
*/

